## 📁 Project Structure

```
network-analyzer/
├── sentinel.py              # Entry point — menu loop, CLI args
├── config.yaml              # Configuration settings
├── requirements.txt         # Python dependencies
├── rules/                   # YAML threat detection rules
│   ├── syn_scan.yaml
│   ├── cleartext.yaml
│   ├── dns_exfil.yaml
│   ├── arp_spoof.yaml
│   └── high_port.yaml
├── core/                    # Engine — capture, decode, scan
│   ├── sniffer.py           # Scapy live capture (threaded)
│   ├── processor.py         # Packet decoding
│   ├── stats.py             # Statistics aggregation
│   ├── scanner.py           # Nmap integration
│   └── pcap_loader.py       # PCAP file loader
├── detection/               # Threat detection
│   ├── rule_engine.py       # YAML rule matcher
│   ├── anomaly.py           # Entropy & pattern detection
│   ├── arp_monitor.py       # ARP spoof detection
│   └── alerts.py            # Alert queue manager
├── network/                 # Network intelligence
│   ├── whois_lookup.py      # IP Whois enrichment
│   ├── traceroute.py        # Path mapping
│   └── resolver.py          # DNS resolution
├── storage/                 # Persistence & export
│   ├── database.py          # SQLite database
│   ├── models.py            # Shared data classes
│   └── exporter.py          # CSV/PCAP/JSON export
├── tui/                     # Terminal UI
│   ├── menu.py              # Main menu & prompts
│   ├── dashboard.py         # Live capture dashboard
│   ├── scan_view.py         # Scan results display
│   ├── pcap_view.py         # PCAP analysis display
│   ├── history_view.py      # History browser
│   └── helpers.py           # Formatting utilities
└── utils/                   # Shared utilities
    ├── constants.py          # Port mappings, colors
    ├── privileges.py         # Admin/root checks
    └── privacy.py            # IP masking
```

---

## 🔧 Custom Detection Rules

Create YAML files in the `rules/` directory:

```yaml
name: "My Custom Rule"
description: "Detect suspicious traffic pattern"
severity: WARNING    # INFO, WARNING, HIGH, CRITICAL
match:
  protocol: TCP
  dst_port: [4444, 5555]
  condition: port_match
action:
  alert: true
  log: true
  message: "Suspicious connection: {src_ip} → {dst_ip}:{dst_port}"
```

Rules are loaded automatically at startup. No code changes required.

